Phase 0 – Learn the foundations (1–2 weeks)

Before writing your app, learn the basics.

Step 1: Learn Git

You'll use Git every day as a software engineer.

Topics:

What Git is
Repositories
Commits
Branches
Pull requests (later)
GitHub

Practice:

Create a GitHub account.
Create your first repository.
Make changes and commit them.
Step 2: Learn TypeScript

Don't skip this.

Learn:

Variables
Functions
Objects
Arrays
Interfaces
Classes
Loops
Async/await
Modules

By the end, you should be able to write small programs comfortably.

Step 3: Learn React

React Native is based on React, so understanding React first makes learning React Native much easier.

Learn:

Components
JSX
Props
State
Event handling
useState
useEffect
Lists
Conditional rendering

Build a few simple web apps to practice these ideas.

Phase 1 – Set up your development environment

Install:

Node.js
VS Code
Git
Android Studio (for the Android emulator)
Expo Go (on your Android or iPhone)

We'll use Expo because it's the easiest way to start with React Native.

Your first app will simply display:

Welcome to Exploring Careers

When you see that on your phone, you've completed your first milestone.

Phase 2 – Learn React Native

Build a few small practice apps before starting your main project.

Practice App 1

Counter App

Learn:

Buttons
State
Styling
Practice App 2

To-do List

Learn:

Lists
Forms
TextInput
Deleting items
Practice App 3

Weather App

Learn:

APIs
Fetch
Loading states
Error handling

After these, you'll be ready for your main project.

Phase 3 – Start Exploring Careers

Create a new project.

